---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'; import {data} from '../data/provider';
const grades=[['E0','Resemblance terminology only','The resemblance is recorded in the literature without an explicit mimicry claim or supporting data.'],['E1','Explicit author proposal','A cited author explicitly proposes the interaction as mimicry, without further support.'],['E2','Ecological, geographic or behavioral support','Distribution, seasonality or behavior is consistent with the proposed mimicry.'],['E3','Quantitative or experimental resemblance or receiver response','Measurements or experiments demonstrate the resemblance or a receiver response to it.'],['E4','Direct experimental biological outcome','Experiments demonstrate the biological outcome of the interaction for mimic or receiver.']];
const interactions=data.all(); const total=interactions.length;
const counts=grades.map(([g])=>interactions.filter(i=>i.evidence===g).length);
const max=Math.max(...counts,1);
---
<Layout><div class="container py-12"><h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Evidence grades</h1><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">Every record carries an evidence grade from the E0–E4 framework. Reporting a resemblance is not equivalent to demonstrating mimicry — the grade makes that distinction explicit. Curators record a reason and an evidence passage; grades are never assigned by keywords alone.</p>
<h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Grade distribution</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Across the {total} labeled demo records — this shows the framework, not a scientific result.</p><div class="card mt-4 p-5">{grades.map(([g],idx)=>{const c=counts[idx];return <div class="flex items-center gap-3 py-1"><span class="pill w-10 text-center">{g}</span><div class="flex-1 h-4 rounded bg-slate-100 overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full bg-teal" style={`width:${Math.round(c/max*100)}%`}></div></div><span class="text-sm text-slate-600 w-24">{c} record{c===1?'':'s'}</span></div>;})}</div>
<h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Definitions</h2><div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">{grades.map(([g,label,desc])=><div class="card flex gap-4"><span class="pill h-fit">{g}</span><div><div class="font-semibold">{label}</div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">{desc}</p></div></div>)}</div><p class="mt-8 text-sm text-slate-600">Full policy: <a href="https://github.com/ZyYang0124/MimicryDB/blob/main/docs/EVIDENCE_GUIDELINES.md">docs/EVIDENCE_GUIDELINES.md</a></p></div></Layout>
